s="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAINIPPON PRINTING CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAI NIPPON PRINTING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA, KEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA, KEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In a liquid crystal display (10), a non-polarized light from a light source (12) is directed through a linear polarization separation layer (14) into a liquid crystal cell (16). In accordance with application of an electric field, the liquid crystal cell (16) changes the direction of a director and accordingly the direction of a field vibration vector of the incident linearly-polarized light by substantially 0 to 90 degrees and causes the changed linearly-polarized light to enter a dichroic linear polarization layer (18) on the surface, so that only the component aligning with the polarization transmission axis may emerge to the outside. The dichroic linear polarization layer (18) transmits 50 % of the extraneous light incident thereon while absorbing the remainder.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un afficheur (10) à cristaux liquides dans lequel une lumière non polarisée provenant d'une source lumineuse est dirigée à travers une couche (14) séparatrice de polarisation rectiligne dans une cellule (16) à cristaux liquides. L'application d'un champ électrique modifie l'angle d'orientation des cellules (16) de cristaux liquide et par conséquent l'orientation du vecteur de vibration de champ de la lumière incidente à polarisation rectiligne de 0 à 90 degrés environ et entraîne la pénétration de la lumière modifiée polarisée de manière rectiligne dans une couche (18) de polarisation rectiligne dichroïque appliquée sur la surface de sorte que seul le composant aligné sur l'axe de transmission de polarisation peut émerger à l'extérieur. La couche (18) de polarisation rectiligne dichroïque transmet 50 % de la lumière incidente arrivant depuis une source externe et absorbe le reste.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>